photonicat-pm (1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the response to a PMU power button press configurable. The new
    pmu-button-mode device tree property selects poweroff (the previous
    hardcoded behavior, still the default), input (report KEY_POWER on an
    input device and let userspace decide, so HandlePowerKey= in
    logind.conf applies to this button), or ignore.
  * Add a button_mode module parameter that overrides the device tree
    property, so a mode can be tried without a device tree overlay and a
    reboot.
  * Document that the PMU never announces a button release, so userspace
    sees every press as a short press.
  * After a press in input or ignore mode, suppress the protocol ACK and
    re-send the watchdog configuration every 30 seconds to try to defer
    the PMU's force shutdown.
  * Record RA2E1260702000 button behavior: presses shorter than about
    three seconds send nothing, and the PMU cuts power about 60 seconds
    after announcing a press regardless of the host's response.

 -- HackingGate <i@hackinggate.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:30:00 +0900

photonicat-pm (1.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Expose the PMU charge stop threshold as the standard battery power
    supply attribute charge_control_end_threshold (50-100%).
  * Expose the PMU power-on mode as power_on_mode, reading unconfigured,
    enabled, or disabled.
  * Report both features through the runtime capability policy, with new
    pmu_charge_threshold_capability and pmu_power_on_mode_capability
    attributes.
  * Block raw CHARGE_THRESHOLD_SET and POWER_ON_MODE_V2_SET frames on
    /dev/pcat-pm-ctl so the exported state cannot drift from the PMU.
  * Document that RA2E1260702000 refuses VOLTAGE_THRESHOLD_SET for every
    payload tested, so the driver does not send it.
  * Strip duplicated and low-information text from README.md and
    pcat-pm-ctl(4), and say PMU firmware consistently where the docs
    previously alternated with MCU firmware.
  * Fix pcat-pm-ctl(4) rendering a literal backslash in the
    force-poweroff-timeout ranges, and correct the examples for the status
    LED acknowledgment delay and the network LED repeat count.
  * Point the frame-format cross-references at the README protocol section
    rather than the man page, which documents command definitions instead.
  * Check man page rendering and README anchors from pre-commit, and track
    pre-commit hook revisions with dependabot.
  * Move the per-firmware observed results to the project wiki. README.md
    and pcat-pm-ctl(4) now describe current firmware behavior only and link
    to the wiki for older versions.

 -- HackingGate <i@hackinggate.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 23:52:07 +0900

photonicat-pm (1.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Document verified PMU firmware RA2E1260515000 RTC behavior.
  * Document current battery and control-device ABI, including computed
    power_now, absent energy_now, and static energy_full behavior.
  * Reject out-of-range fan cooling states before sending PMU FAN_SET
    commands.

