photonicat-pm (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Forward PMU hardware and firmware version acknowledgment frames to
    /dev/pcat-pm-ctl so unmodified pcat-pmu-updater version queries can read
    PMU replies.
  * Serialize raw-control input separately from output delivery so PMU ACK
    frames remain readable by /dev/pcat-pm-ctl userspace consumers.
  * Align battery capacity parsing with the vendor driver: PMU protocol v2
    status reports use PMU-reported SOC, while shorter status reports use OCV
    fallback from the battery profile.
  * Remove the experimental stuck-100% SOC override so PMU protocol v2 capacity
    reporting matches the vendor parser.
  * Gate PMU behavior through runtime validation and keep /dev/rtc0 registered
    while RTC reads and scheduled boot stay disabled until valid, advancing PMU
    RTC samples are observed.
  * Expose the runtime RTC policy state through pmu_rtc_capability and enable
    PMU-backed RTC wakeups once validation promotes RTC support.
  * Document the PMU firmware capability policy without using version strings as
    feature gates.

 -- HackingGate <i@hackinggate.com>  Sun, 17 May 2026 14:33:17 +0900

photonicat-pm (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix battery capacity reporting when PMU firmware RA2E1260306000 reports
    a stuck 100% state of charge while the pack is still charging.
  * Preserve older PMU firmware behavior by only applying the stuck-SOC quirk
    to the affected firmware version.
  * Use the battery design capacity for ENERGY_FULL instead of unsupported PMU
    status report energy fields.

